identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21794565
    description: "Concept DOI, resolves to the latest version"
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21794566
    description: >-
      Version DOI for v1.0.0. Superseded: v1.0.0 predates decisions D035-D042
      and carries the 20-state subsample values and an unreproducible
      normalisation contrast. Cite the concept DOI above, or the v1.1.0 version
      DOI below.
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21798343
    description: >-
      Version DOI for v1.1.0. Superseded: v1.1.0 predates the Hopf result
      (D046), the fold-orientation classification, the adoption of v5 as the
      manuscript source, and the beta-range correction (D047-D048). It also
      predates Phases A-C entirely, and is the last version Zenodo holds: its
      record still carries the earlier "collapse threshold" title (D072).
  # v1.2.0 was TAGGED but never deposited. Zenodo mints on a GitHub Release and
  # not on a tag, so no version DOI exists for it and none is written here.
  # The v2.0.0 version DOI is minted on deposit and added afterwards. Both
  # absences are deliberate rather than guessed: a DOI written before it exists
  # is a fabricated identifier.
abstract: >-
  Derivation, verification and numerical study of the fold condition of a
  finite-resource proteostasis clearance network. The saddle-node of the
  two-state conserved-resource model is shown to be exactly a constrained
  critical point of total removal flux on the aggregate nullcline, giving the
  identity det J = -(grad R x grad G), with an n-state generalisation and
  corollaries for growth dilution and for self-damaging clearance machinery.
keywords:
  - proteostasis
  - saddle-node bifurcation
  - conserved resource
  - protein aggregation
  - mathematical biology
